> Also having the same issue but with qwen 3.8 27b with hicache

[Original comment](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37619#issuecomment-5566232515)

@Sichrono This update skips an optional unfinished-request checkpoint when eviction cannot supply a Mamba slot. The request keeps its KV indices instead of crashing the scheduler. Two CPU regression tests pass; this update has not been tested with the reported Qwen HiCache workload.

> Happy to test this branch on the same deployment/workload if that helps move it forward.

[Original comment](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37619#issuecomment-5606493113)

@leehom0123 Rebased onto main `c7be3e935b5`. Failed unfinished-checkpoint allocation now takes the existing zero-length insertion path and keeps the request's KV indices. Two CPU regression tests pass, including an exhausted-allocation case that fails on unpatched main. This update has not been tested with the reported Qwen HiCache workload.

